Day 5 takeaway (Part 2/2) -

Simple Jenkinsfile (Declarative Pipeline)

pipeline {
    agent any   // Run on any available Jenkins agent

    stages {
        stage('Checkout') {
            steps {
                // Get source code from Git
                git branch: 'main', url: 'https://lnkd.in/db7UYsyx'
            }
        }

        stage('Build') {
            steps {
                echo '📦 Building the project...'
                sh 'npm install'   // Example for Node.js project
            }
        }

        stage('Test') {
            steps {
                echo '🧪 Running tests...'
                sh 'npm test'
            }
        }

        stage('Deploy') {
            when {
                branch 'main'   // Only deploy from main branch
            }
            steps {
                echo '🚀 Deploying application...'
                // Example: sh './deploy.sh'
            }
        }
    }

    post {
        always {
            echo '✅ Pipeline finished.'
        }
    }
}


🔎 What this Jenkins pipeline does:
Checkout: Pulls code from GitHub (main branch).
Build: Installs dependencies.
Test: Runs automated tests.
Deploy: Only runs on the main branch (like GitHub Actions).
Post: Always runs after pipeline (success or failure).
